2. Master Installer (Fresh Build List)

Run these blocks in sequence on a clean Alpine LXC to replicate the current successful state.

Phase 1: Dependencies & Baseline

apk update && apk upgrade
apk add curl wget bash openresty nodejs npm python3 sqlite htop nano net-tools git openrc
rc-update add devfs boot


Phase 2: Grafana Network Exposure

apk add grafana
rc-update add grafana default
# Inject environment overrides to bypass .ini limitations
echo 'export GF_SERVER_HTTP_ADDR=0.0.0.0' > /etc/conf.d/grafana
echo 'export GF_SERVER_HTTP_PORT=3000' >> /etc/conf.d/grafana
# Ensure the config file matches
sed -i 's/^;http_addr =.*/http_addr = 0.0.0.0/' /etc/grafana.ini
rc-service grafana restart


Phase 3: Nginx Proxy Manager Native Build (FIXED URL)

# 1. Setup Directory and Clone (Clean Shell Version)
mkdir -p /var/www/npm && cd /var/www/npm
# Use direct URL to avoid shell bracket/parenthesis errors
git clone [https://github.com/NginxProxyManager/nginx-proxy-manager.git](https://github.com/NginxProxyManager/nginx-proxy-manager.git) .

# 2. Build Backend (Compilation Phase)
# MUST be inside the /backend directory for npm to find package.json
cd /var/www/npm/backend
npm install --omit=dev

# 3. Persistence Service
cat <<EOF > /etc/init.d/npm-admin
#!/sbin/openrc-run
description="NPM Admin UI"
command="/usr/bin/node"
command_args="/var/www/npm/backend/index.js"
directory="/var/www/npm/backend"
pidfile="/run/npm-admin.pid"
background="yes"
EOF
chmod +x /etc/init.d/npm-admin
rc-update add npm-admin default
service npm-admin start


